# LIVE INSTALLER ONLY — never shipped on the installed system.
#
# The live USB (LIVE_INSTALLER=1 base) runs the Quickshell installer + GParted from the `dev` autologin
# Wayland session, which has NO polkit agent and NO owner account yet, so passwordless sudo is its only
# escalation path (shrek-live-welcome / shrek-install-run do `sudo -n`). The live medium is an ephemeral,
# single-purpose whole-disk-erase tool with no persistent state, so broad NOPASSWD here is acceptable and
# unavoidable pre-owner-account.
#
# `scripts/build-in-container.sh` installs this file into the sealed base /etc ONLY for LIVE_INSTALLER
# builds; every other variant (INSTALLABLE = the product, DOGFOOD = the proof, plain CI) removes it, so the
# installed system ships a `dev` account with NO passwordless root (bench authz slice step 4). The generated
# copy at image/overlay/etc/sudoers.d/dev-nopasswd is gitignored. sudoers.d files must be mode 0440.
#
# Full retirement of the placeholder identity (the baked `dev` account itself + a real owner-authority
# subject) awaits the owner-account provisioning wizard — see docs/installer-0.md and docs/bench-authz-step4-nopasswd-retire.md.
dev ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL
